  "solution": {
    "explanation": "Define dp[i][j] as the LCS length of the first i characters of text1 and first j of text2. If the characters match, extend the diagonal: dp[i-1][j-1] + 1; otherwise take the better of dropping a character from either string. Filling the table is O(m*n) time, and since each row needs only the one above, O(n) space. Exponential recursion without memoisation fails on 1000-character inputs.",
    "code": "class Solution:\n    def longestCommonSubsequence(self, text1: str, text2: str) -> int:\n        prev = [0] * (len(text2) + 1)\n        for a in text1:\n            cur = [0]\n            for j, b in enumerate(text2):\n                if a == b:\n                    cur.append(prev[j] + 1)\n                else:\n                    cur.append(max(prev[j + 1], cur[j]))\n            prev = cur\n        return prev[-1]\n"
  }
